---
title: Pad kra prao
servings: 2
yield: 2 to 3 servings
tags: [chicken, stir-fry, quick]
cuisine: thai
source: Pad Kra Pao (Pad Gaprao) Chicken Stir-Fry with Holy Basil by Pailin Chongchitnant, Hot Thai Kitchen, https://hot-thai-kitchen.com/holy-basil-stir-fry
---

== Stir-fry ==

Pound the @Thai chiles{5-10} to a fine paste in a #mortar and pestle{}. Add the @garlic{5%cloves} and @spur chilies{1}(chopped; or another mild red chile) and pound to a rough paste.

Stir together @oyster sauce{1%tbsp}, @soy sauce{1%tbsp}, @fish sauce{2%tsp}, @black soy sauce{1 1/2%tsp}, @water{2%tbsp} and @sugar{1 1/2%tsp} until the sugar dissolves.

Fry the chile paste in a little @vegetable oil{} in a #wok{} over medium-high heat until the garlic starts to turn golden.

Add the @chicken{300%g}(minced) and break it up. Pour in the sauce and toss until the chicken is nearly done.

Add the @onion{1/2}(small, diced) and @long beans{1/2%cup}(cut short) and toss until the chicken is cooked.

Off the heat, stir in the @holy basil leaves{1 1/2%cup}(loosely packed). Taste and adjust.

== Fried eggs ==

Heat about 1 cm of @vegetable oil{} in a small #non-stick pan{} over medium-high heat until very hot.

Crack in the @eggs{2-3}(one per person) and fry until the edges are brown and crisp. Serve on rice with the stir-fry.

> For a table sauce, stir chopped Thai chiles and garlic into fish sauce with a squeeze of lime.
